Place these DLLs in a directory and then run:
regsvr32 npFujiCMPlugin.dll
to register the DLL with Firefox and IE, and Safari

Unfortunately, the EyeOneIO.dll loads the EyeOne.dll in a way that looses the path it was running
in.  This means the EyeOne.dll must be copied to the Windows/System32 directory during installation.

The Techkon devices are not driven through a traditional SDK.  The driver is a TCP connected service
and the plugin uses TCP to connect to it at run time.
 
For each type of scanner there is a different sample to keep things simple.
In theory one htm/javascript could work with them all by checking for
type.

The examples are in "webexamples":

SpectroJet.htm - Techkon SpectroJet example using the Sync150 chart
                 NOTE:  On the first line, the light cyan will not be recognized as part
                        of the strip in REmoveScanBoundries mode.  There is not sufficient
                        contrast. The example however first tries with RemoveScanBoundries set to
			"True", then if that fails tries it with "False" and this appears to work.

i1.htm         - This is an example for the X-Rite i1 hand strip scanner using the Sync150 chart.

iO.htm         - This is an example for the X-Rite i0 robotic scanner using the first page of the
                 random330 test chart.
iSisExample.htm - This is a test file for the X-Rite iSis chart reader.  The example chart is the
                  isis test chart provided in the sdk.
